# Who must approve a pull request, by path. The last matching line wins for
# each file, and every owner matched by the pull request must approve.
#
# This mirrors the review tiers in .app_checks.exs, which `mix app.checks`
# uses to print the tier of a branch and to keep protected files alone in
# their pull request. Keep the two files in step. See
# docs/patterns/code-review.md.
#
# Replace @org/engineers and @org/architects with your teams. Make architects
# members of engineers too, so one architect approval satisfies both lines.

# standard: every file needs an engineer
*                                        @org/engineers

# low: no owner, so the one approval the branch rule requires can come from
# the automated reviewer
/lib/example_web/live/**/*.heex
/lib/example_web/controllers/**/*.heex
/docs/
/README.md

# high
/lib/example_web.ex                      @org/architects
/lib/example_web/components/             @org/architects
/lib/example_web/router.ex               @org/architects
/lib/example_web/endpoint.ex             @org/architects
/lib/example/application.ex              @org/architects
/config/                                 @org/architects
/mix.exs                                 @org/architects
/mix.lock                                @org/architects
/.tool-versions                          @org/architects
/test/support/                           @org/architects
/.github/                                @org/architects

# protected, also kept alone in their pull request by mix app.checks
/AGENTS.md                               @org/architects
/.github/CODEOWNERS                      @org/architects
/.github/workflows/protected-*           @org/architects
/.credo.exs                              @org/architects
/.check.exs                              @org/architects
/.app_checks.exs                         @org/architects
/priv/checks/                            @org/architects
/lib/mix/tasks/app.checks.ex             @org/architects
